{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "26105582",
      "title": "Working with Interfaces",
      "lectureOrder": 760,
      "videoOrder": 700,
      "sourceHash": "d38db2bcc06cd99411d2df8142fa553de854567b39644c8eedd554948b2f669e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "Narrator: Now, another important feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 8.22,
          "en": "kind of related to classes and objects in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.22,
          "end": 12.409,
          "en": "is the interfaces feature, and that's a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.409,
          "end": 15.067,
          "en": "which only exists in TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.067,
          "end": 19.56,
          "en": "not in vanilla JavaScript, and any interface code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.56,
          "end": 21.96,
          "en": "which you write- which you'll see in a second-",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.96,
          "end": 25.383,
          "en": "will therefore not be compiled to JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 29.592,
          "en": "Now, what are interfaces? In their most basic form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.592,
          "end": 34.265,
          "en": "interfaces are really just object type definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.265,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "So we could say that we have a Human object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 42.12,
          "en": "in our application, and we can define it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.12,
          "end": 46.53,
          "en": "with the interface keyword, then curly braces thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.53,
          "end": 49.68,
          "en": "and now here, between those curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 52.289,
          "en": "we can define the structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.289,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "the type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "of any Human object we wanna create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 59.85,
          "en": "So we could say a Human should have a first name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.85,
          "end": 63.63,
          "en": "which is a string, and should maybe have an age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.63,
          "end": 66.3,
          "en": "which is a number, and then let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.3,
          "end": 71.3,
          "en": "every Human should also have a method to greet other humans.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.31,
          "end": 74.16,
          "en": "And for this, we can add \"greet\" here, but, now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.16,
          "end": 78.6,
          "en": "very important, we don't add the methods definition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.6,
          "end": 82.65,
          "en": "we don't add the actual code that goes into that method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.65,
          "end": 86.31,
          "en": "but instead just the type of that method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 89.643,
          "en": "which we can do like this, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.87,
          "end": 92.67,
          "en": "Now, we're saying that every Human",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.67,
          "end": 97.28999999999999,
          "en": "should have a \"greet\" method, which actually is a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 100.503,
          "en": "that takes no parameters and returns nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 101.82,
          "end": 104.64,
          "en": "Now we can use this interface, as I just said,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.64,
          "end": 108.78,
          "en": "as an object type. So if I have a new variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.78,
          "end": 111.50999999999999,
          "en": "named Max, because I wanna store information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 114.459,
          "en": "about myself in there, then I could make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.459,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "that this should be a type Human, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 121.38,
          "en": "And now if I wanna assign a value, I'm not allowed to store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.38,
          "end": 124.496,
          "en": "a number, I am allowed to store an object but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.496,
          "end": 128.55,
          "en": "only an object that has this structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.55,
          "end": 130.68,
          "en": "And I now also get auto completion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "and I have to make it clear that there is a first name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 137.91,
          "en": "an age, and now I have to add a \"greet\" method as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 137.91,
          "end": 140.52,
          "en": "And here we now have the actual code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 140.52,
          "end": 144.84,
          "en": "not the type definition. And now this works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 144.84,
          "end": 147.34,
          "en": "because this object, which has store in Max,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.34,
          "end": 152.34,
          "en": "fulfills the requirements set forth by that interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 156.96,
          "en": "So we can use interfaces to define object types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "but we could also do this with the type keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 164.643,
          "en": "to create an alias- like this- that would work as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.54,
          "end": 167.61,
          "en": "So why do we have interfaces then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 167.61,
          "end": 169.923,
          "en": "if we can do the same with the type keyword?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 170.76,
          "end": 173.46,
          "en": "Well, for one, of course, interfaces are simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 173.46,
          "end": 176.7,
          "en": "an alternative, and you can use interfaces instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 176.7,
          "end": 180.38,
          "en": "of the type keyword when you wanna define object types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 180.38,
          "end": 183.509,
          "en": "but they also have one other extra feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.509,
          "end": 186.96,
          "en": "which the type keyword does not give you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.96,
          "end": 190.798,
          "en": "Interfaces can be implemented by classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 190.798,
          "end": 195.798,
          "en": "and when they are, they force classes to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 195.9,
          "end": 198.9,
          "en": "that structure defined by the interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.9,
          "end": 201.09,
          "en": "Now this might sound very abstract,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.09,
          "end": 204.32999999999998,
          "en": "but this can be helpful if you're building an application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 204.32999999999998,
          "end": 206.88,
          "en": "with multiple developers and you wanna ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 206.88,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "that a certain class written by another developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 212.087,
          "en": "has a certain structure because you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 212.087,
          "end": 216,
          "en": "for your part you're working on, need that class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 216,
          "end": 218.21699999999998,
          "en": "to have that structure- you need that class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.21699999999998,
          "end": 221.01,
          "en": "to have a certain method, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.01,
          "end": 222.84,
          "en": "And it's the same for Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.84,
          "end": 225.095,
          "en": "Angular, as you will see in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 225.095,
          "end": 228.6,
          "en": "also has a couple of interfaces which we will use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 228.6,
          "end": 230.22,
          "en": "from time to time in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 230.22,
          "end": 233.524,
          "en": "which then force us to add certain features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.524,
          "end": 236.79,
          "en": "to the classes we define, and we will work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 240.36,
          "en": "with a lot of classes when we are working with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 240.36,
          "end": 244.05,
          "en": "And Angular gives up interfaces that force us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 246.75,
          "en": "to add certain features to our classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 246.75,
          "end": 249.6,
          "en": "so that it then is able to use these classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.6,
          "end": 253.11,
          "en": "correctly internally. And you'll see all of that in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 253.11,
          "end": 256.053,
          "en": "throughout the course. Now I'll give you an example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 256.053,
          "end": 260.1,
          "en": "Let's say I add a new class here, \"Instructor\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 260.1,
          "end": 264.435,
          "en": "and I wanna make sure that this class has this shape,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 264.435,
          "end": 267.66,
          "en": "because someone else who's working on the team",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.66,
          "end": 270.33,
          "en": "needs that class to have that shape.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 270.33,
          "end": 273.24,
          "en": "Then we can add the implements keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 273.24,
          "end": 276.6,
          "en": "and implement our interface before we add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 276.6,
          "end": 280.35,
          "en": "the curly braces to start defining the class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 280.35,
          "end": 283.23,
          "en": "And now because I'm implementing this interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 283.23,
          "end": 285.42,
          "en": "I'm getting some red squiggly lines here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 285.42,
          "end": 290.15999999999997,
          "en": "and I'm being forced to correctly implement this interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.15999999999997,
          "end": 292.86,
          "en": "which means I have to add the first name property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 292.86,
          "end": 296.28,
          "en": "of type string here, I have to add an age property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.28,
          "end": 300.03,
          "en": "of type number here, and I have to add a \"greet\" method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.03,
          "end": 303.78,
          "en": "And only if I add all of that, no matter which exact code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 303.78,
          "end": 306.36,
          "en": "I then have in that greet method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 306.36,
          "end": 309.75,
          "en": "but only after I add the general structure here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 309.75,
          "end": 313.74,
          "en": "this error goes away because I'm now correctly implementing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 313.74,
          "end": 314.733,
          "en": "this interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 315.69,
          "end": 318.93,
          "en": "And that's another key part of interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 318.93,
          "end": 323.16,
          "en": "They don't just act as object types. Instead, they also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 323.16,
          "end": 328.16,
          "en": "force us to set up a certain structure for our classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 330.656,
          "en": "and that's what we're taking advantage of here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 330.656,
          "end": 333.45,
          "en": "and that's what we'll also see in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 333.45,
          "end": 334.683,
          "en": "throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
